[{:db/id 17592186179821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c2277e51-aeb9-59a4-9f7f-011ebd2053af" "question-bebcf13b-8bc8-52b9-bfbb-3d010d1e3235" "question-145c5319-64c4-5787-bd03-fd6d4dc74190" "question-9a2bd275-71a9-5205-b152-299bcdd3fc0a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179450 :question/problem "Calculate $(-9 ) \\cdot (-5).$" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of two negative numbers, $\\color{red}-9$ and ${\\color{red}-5}.$ So the product will be positive:\n![](images/17/1793b9f5cb618eb1fe60e0ea34ce271a42e44ca04e92d7546289239fffee2a40.svg)\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $9$ and $5$ without any signs: $9 \\cdot 5 = 45.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-9)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}45}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179822 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-edd9589d-5442-58a3-84f8-fb0a90d9d945" "question-6db7b1f8-571b-596f-b937-087002cb4535" "question-bd957b0c-87c0-5c1c-877a-535c72909197" "question-dcae9997-c063-556b-b99d-bfc224ab7e6d" "question-515d2e58-90d5-54f6-8477-014fb0487556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179451 :question/problem "What is the value of $(-3) \\cdot (-5) \\cdot (-10)?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by multiplying the first two numbers. We have the product of two negatives, which gives a positive: \n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)} = {\\color{blue}15}.\n$$\n\nSo we now have\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{{\\color{red}(-3)} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-5)}}_{\\large {\\color{blue}15}} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)}.\n$$\n\nThen, we work out this remaining product using the fact that a positive times a negative gives a negative:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}15} \\cdot {\\color{red}(-10)} = {\\color{red}-(15\\cdot 10)} = {\\color{red}-150}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179823 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4c3a1d41-b0b4-56cb-9c22-249c40340608" "question-c193a4aa-2a3b-50a7-9351-eac6230e1fa9" "question-3cfaf2ea-e7d3-519a-880f-3892d2b32646" "question-2ffab9e9-5351-5fcd-b618-932668f56d97" "question-319279a3-ba94-5bbe-b88b-0e4da5c9c0b6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179452 :question/problem "Calculate ![](images/5b/5bc84ed7352b634beafa94e49a471b572e749307630e34e1e6f24a3c9ba2e177.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of two negative numbers, so the product will be positive, and we can drop the minus signs as follows:\n![](images/76/7687ac2259cb4c0e43ef7899fba49d37133444905fdde539e6278cbdf7a5c81a.svg)\n\nNow, we multiply the fractions by multiplying the numerators and denominators separately:\n\n![](images/1c/1cb412aef30a8b0dda2368ea1d8529fc3c5ba33a263e909ac1f476a47502c116.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179824 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-475b778e-4110-57c0-909a-94c0d0c3f398" "question-c5da7489-1e96-592e-8ffe-aaecfa0d4fb2" "question-6e4f8c55-ff7a-58f7-9342-3b5b8d2c1065" "question-f9693f01-1b7b-566f-8d4a-ee5e7f15cd38"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179453 :question/problem "What is $(-3.4) \\cdot 3.8?$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c2277e51-aeb9-59a4-9f7f-011ebd2053af" :question/id #uuid "c2277e51-aeb9-59a4-9f7f-011ebd2053af" :question/math-academy-id "q-128394" :question/problem "$(-7)\\cdot (-3)=$" :question/worked-solution "We have a product of two negative numbers, $-7$ and $-3.$ So the product will be positive:\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we multiply $7$ and $3$ without any signs: $7\\cdot 3=21.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n(-7)\\cdot (-3)=21.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c8a6d378-d941-5860-a06d-dd3f1bc986e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c8a6d378-d941-5860-a06d-dd3f1bc986e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8a6d378-d941-5860-a06d-dd3f1bc986e4" :answe